cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this verification artifact, please cite the specific archived version you
  checked, not the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the
  "Archival" section in README.md.
title: >-
  minimal-uniformity-three: machine-checked companion to "Minimal uniformity three:
  unit-edge tilings around the non-Archimedean vertex types"
abstract: >-
  The verification artifact for the paper's claims: the U(z) minimal-uniformity ladder
  (the k = 1 scan, the k <= 2 catalogue and refutation, the four rigid uniformity-3
  witnesses, the essential-irregularity verdicts), re-derived in exact rational and
  cyclotomic arithmetic, and the k <= 2 DRAT completeness certificate — 24 UNSAT
  obligations over the tier-1 certification universe, kissat-solved and
  drat-trim-verified. The repository holds only the claim specs; all machinery is the
  pinned research-core library.
type: software
authors:
